-- Horus Platform — Master Specification Index
-- ======================================================
--
-- This directory contains the formal Allium specification for the
-- Horus AI-Powered Aviation Training Platform.
--
-- File inventory:
--   core.allium      — Identity, tenancy, organizations, users, seats, RBAC
--   training.allium  — Scenarios, training sessions, voice logs, modules
--   content.allium   — Content articles, assessments, badges, leaderboards
--   flight.allium    — Flight plans, legs, waypoints, performance logs
--   surfaces.allium  — API boundary surfaces (Hangar, Tower, Squawk)
--
-- Quick start:
--   1. Read core.allium first ( foundational domain )
--   2. Read training.allium ( primary training flow )
--   3. Read content.allium + flight.allium ( supporting domains )
--   4. Read surfaces.allium ( API contracts )
--
-- Cross-module references:
--   - core/Organization is the tenancy root
--   - core/User is the identity root
--   - core/Seat binds users to organizations with roles
--   - training/Scenario and content/ContentArticle are org-scoped content
--   - training/TrainingSession is the primary runtime entity
--   - content/AssessmentResult and flight/FlightHourLog capture outcomes
--
-- Config values:
--   max_seats_per_org: Integer = 50
--   default_session_timeout: Duration = 30.minutes
--   invitation_expiry: Duration = 7.days
--
-- Open questions:
--   - Should flight plans require a linked scenario, or be independent?
--   - Should instructor ratings be public within the org?
--   - Should leaderboard snapshots be auto-generated or on-demand?
